{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For laughter</b>. But they see that all joy in the world and laughter — their essence is in bread that workers make, and wine that gladdens a person's life. And it is possible that חיים is an epithet, for wine gladdens the living that are upon the face of the earth. And silver יענה את הכל (answers all), and the meaning of יענה is 'provides'; and it is possible that it is from עת (time), as I explained, and the meaning is that it provides it at the time the desirer desires."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:03.786675373Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}